    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d358-a1">

                <pb facs="0398" n="322" sameAs="frus:frus1916/pg322"/>

                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Inclosure 1—Translation]</seg>
                </opener>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">Ratification by the President</hi>
                </head>
                <p>Regarding as acceptable the convention signed on September 16, 1915, between the
                    Government of Haiti and that of the United States of America, represented by Mr.
                    Louis Borno, Secretary of State for Foreign Relations, and Mr. Robert Beale
                    Davis, Jr., Chargé d Affaires, respectively.</p>
                <p>We hereby declare our approval, ratification and confirmation of the said
                    convention and promise and cause it to be executed and observed according to its
                    form and tenor without permitting any contravention thereof.</p>
                <p>In faith whereof, we have signed with our own hand the present ratification and
                    caused the seal of the Republic to be affixed thereto.</p>
                <closer>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-left">Given at the <placeName><placeName
                                type="venue">National Palace</placeName> of <placeName type="city"
                                >Port au Prince</placeName></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1915-09-17">September 17, 1915, the 112th year of
                            Independence</date>.</dateline>
                    <lb/>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Dartiguenave</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
                <postscript>
                    <p>By the President: <lb/>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Louis Borno</hi>, <lb/>
                        <hi rendition="#italic">Secretary of State for Foreign Relations</hi>
                    </p>
                </postscript>
            </div>
